# Line endings.
#
# Why this file exists: the repo's committed content is LF, but the working
# tree drifted to CRLF for most files, so `git status` showed ~40 files as
# fully rewritten and `git diff` with no path was useless for review. With no
# .gitattributes and core.autocrlf unset, nothing was normalising anything.
#
# `text=auto` means: git decides per file whether it is text, and stores text
# as LF in the repository regardless of what the working tree holds. Checkout
# leaves LF here (core.autocrlf is unset), which is what every editor and tool
# in this project already handles — the launcher is Python, the capture UI is
# JS/CSS, and both run fine with LF on Windows.
*               text=auto

# Windows batch files are the one real exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse labels
# and goto targets in an LF-only .bat, so these stay CRLF on disk.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Anything that runs on the Pi must be LF, whatever the laptop does to it.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to "fix" the bytes or diff them as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.bmp           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.mp4           binary
*.avi           binary
*.mov           binary
*.mkv           binary
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.xlsm          binary
*.h5            binary
*.hdf5          binary
*.ttf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
